    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first non‑native settlers arrived in 1652, building a sawmill powered by a waterfall on the Exeter River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brentwood%2C_New_Hampshire"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1742 residents of the southwestern part of Exeter petitioned to become an independent parish, eventually forming Brentwood after a 1742 charter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brentwood%2C_New_Hampshire"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Abenaki Pennacook people farmed, fished, and hunted in the area that is now Brentwood long before European settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
